#!/usr/bin/env perl

use strict;
use warnings;

use FindBin::libs;

use Trog::Auth;
use Trog::Config;

=head1 SYNOPSIS

Print a user's TOTP enrollment details, so that they can set up 2FA without
going through the web UI -- or get back in when they've lost their
authenticator and you need to read them the current code.

=head2 USAGE

    bin/totp username

Prints the otpauth:// URI (what a QR code would encode), the base32 secret to
type into an authenticator by hand, and the code which is valid right now.

Note that this hands out everything needed to generate that user's codes
forever, so treat the output like a password.

=head2 CAVEATS

Requires general.hostname to be set in the tCMS configuration, as the domain is
part of what an authenticator shows the user.  Set it with bin/tcms-hostname.

=cut

my $user   = shift @ARGV;
my $domain = Trog::Config->get()->param('general.hostname');

die "Must provide a user"                   unless $user;
die "Must Set domain in configuration file" unless $domain;

my ( $uri, $qr, $failure, $message, $totp ) = Trog::Auth::totp( $user, $domain );
print "TOTP URI: $uri\n";
print "Secret: " . $totp->base32secret() . "\n";
print "Current Auth code: " . $totp->expected_totp_code(time) . "\n";
